  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">From Policy to Practice: Operationalizing a Rights-Based Approach to Return and Reintegration (RR P2P)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The return and reintegration of migrants is a policy priority for many governments worldwide. As a result, an increasing number of international, regional and sub-regional stakeholders have entered the field or expanded their roles as actors in return migration. In 2021, IOM released the Policy on the Full Spectrum of Return, Readmission and Reintegration (RRR Policy), which guides the work of IOM on return migration through a holistic, rights-based and sustainable development-oriented approach that facilitates safe and dignified return, readmission and sustainable reintegration. The policy focuses on the well-being of individual returnees and the protection of their rights. At the same time, it recognizes that States have a sovereign prerogative to determine their national migration policies and to govern migration within their jurisdiction, in conformity with international law commitments. Having achieved a harmonized policy that sets the ground for a rights-based and migrant-centered approach to RRR, challenges remain in the translation of the policy into tangible actions and operations. Practical tools, designed from lessons learned and a long expertise trajectory particularly in the field of return migration, need to be developed, piloted and implemented to materialize the objectives set forth in IOMs RRR Policy.</narrative>
  </description>
